{"abstract":"To examine the impact of a co-created culturally sensitive diabetes self-management education and support (DSMES) intervention on the physical and mental health of immigrants with type 2 diabetes (T2D). Pre- and post-test among people with T2D whose primary language was Urdu, Arabic or Turkish (n = 97). Participants were offered a six-week intervention based on a person-centred approach using research-based dialogue tools to facilitate learning and reflection, which was developed in co-creation with immigrants and healthcare professionals. Data were collected at baseline, post-intervention and after 6 months and analysed using paired t-tests, Wilcoxon signed-rank tests, chi-square tests and regression models when appropriate. Several clinical outcomes were improved post-intervention, including HbA1c (P < 0.001), body fat percentage (P = 0.002), self-rated general health (P = 0.05), well-being (P = 0.004) and several self-management behaviours, e.g., physical activity (P < 0.001). Most outcomes remained improved after 6 months, but the effect on HbA1c was no longer statistically significant. Some outcomes were improved only at 6 months, including waist circumference (P < 0.001) and diabetes-related emotional distress (P < 0.001). Fatigue did not change. Attendance at more programme sessions was associated with better outcomes. The DSMES intervention developed in a co-creation process was highly effective in improving the health of immigrants with T2D.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hempler, Nana Folmann","Fagt, Charlotte","Olesen, Kasper","Wagner, Sabina","Rasmussen, Lone Banke","Laursen, Ditte Hjorth","Glümer, Charlotte","Nygaard, Mette","Willaing, Ingrid"],"cuid":["S02-095.74-002576"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hempler, Nana Folmann"],"keyword":["ADULTS","CARE","Co creation","Cultural sensitivity","Denmark","Diabetes self management","Immigrants","Mortality","Prevalence","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving health and diabetes self management in immigrants with type 000000000002 diabetes through a co created diabetes self management education and support intervention","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10900-022-01151-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.74-002576","identifier":[{"id":"36326989","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85141145764","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000878476200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9632564","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-339d9fd9-c722-47c8-ba71-19197dc4b30d","ku-fd3a4fe5-7f5e-4277-bc98-9b55187b3309"],"keyword":["ADULTS","CARE","Co-creation","Cultural sensitivity","DENMARK","Diabetes self-management","Immigrants","MORTALITY","PREVALENCE","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-182C49CA3A2D0B322AB4BB4696E18D84"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10900-022-01151-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/531240461/s10900_022_01151_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/337972872/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3n